Cell["windows = {{0.866013, 1.887908}, {0.800156, 1.617708}, {0.869456, 1.878026}, {0.848838, 1.784293}};\nink = RGBColor[0.07, 0.32, 0.36];\nrule = RGBColor[0.78, 0.28, 0.12];\nband = RGBColor[0.95, 0.75, 0.40];\n\nListLinePlot[Transpose[{t1, y1}],\n  PlotStyle -> Directive[ink, AbsoluteThickness[1.7]],\n  Frame -> True, Axes -> False,\n  FrameLabel -> {\"time (s)\", \"distance (m)\"},\n  PlotLabel -> \"Four filters, trial 1\",\n  GridLines -> Automatic,\n  GridLinesStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.88]],\n  PlotRange -> {All, {-0.15, 6.3}},\n  ImageSize -> 540, AspectRatio -> 0.62,\n  LabelStyle -> Directive[Black, 12],\n  Prolog -> {\n    Opacity[0.55], band,\n    Rectangle[{windows[[1, 1]], -0.15}, {windows[[1, 2]], 6.3}]\n  },\n  Epilog -> {\n    Text[Style[\"straight section\", 12, RGBColor[0.35, 0.22, 0.05]], {1.38, 5.55}]\n  }\n]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Best-fit line on the straight section", "Section"],
Cell["The shaded points were passed to LinearModelFit. The model is a straight line, and the slope of that line is the terminal speed. Open circles are the measured points. The orange line is the fit, and the equation printed on the graph is the equation of that line.\n\nFor trial 1 the fit is\n\nd = 2.571 t - 0.815\n\nwith d in meters and t in seconds. The slope is 2.571 m/s. Its standard error is 0.005 m/s, and R^2 on this short section is 0.9998.\n\nThe same reading of the trace, applied to the other three trials, gives these slopes:\n\nTrial 1: 2.571 m/s, from 0.866 s to 1.888 s\nTrial 2: 2.432 m/s, from 0.800 s to 1.618 s\nTrial 3: 2.635 m/s, from 0.869 s to 1.878 s\nTrial 4: 2.535 m/s, from 0.849 s to 1.784 s", "Text"],
Cell["take[t_, y_, w_] := Select[Transpose[{t, y}], w[[1]] - 10^-9 <= #[[1]] <= w[[2]] + 10^-9 &];\nshort = {\n  take[t1, y1, windows[[1]]],\n  take[t2, y2, windows[[2]]],\n  take[t3, y3, windows[[3]]],\n  take[t4, y4, windows[[4]]]\n};\nfits = LinearModelFit[#, x, x] & /@ short;\nslopes = Table[fits[[i]][\"BestFitParameters\"][[2]], {i, 4}];\nintercepts = Table[fits[[i]][\"BestFitParameters\"][[1]], {i, 4}];\nr2short = Table[fits[[i]][\"RSquared\"], {i, 4}];\n\neq1 = \"d = 2.571 t - 0.815\";\n\nColumn[{\n  TableForm[\n    Transpose[{\n      {1, 2, 3, 4},\n      windows[[All, 1]],\n      windows[[All, 2]],\n      slopes,\n      intercepts,\n      r2short\n    }],\n    TableHeadings -> {None, {\"trial\", \"t start (s)\", \"t end (s)\", \"slope (m/s)\", \"intercept (m)\", \"R^2\"}}\n  ],\n  Show[\n    Plot[fits[[1]][x], {x, windows[[1, 1]], windows[[1, 2]]},\n      PlotStyle -> Directive[rule, AbsoluteThickness[2.2]]\n    ],\n    ListPlot[short[[1]],\n      PlotMarkers -> {\n        Graphics[{EdgeForm[Directive[ink, Thickness[0.14]]], FaceForm[White], Disk[{0, 0}, 1]}],\n        0.032\n      }\n    ],\n    Frame -> True, Axes -> False,\n    FrameLabel -> {\"time (s)\", \"distance (m)\"},\n    PlotLabel -> \"Trial 1, straight section and best-fit line\",\n    GridLines -> Automatic,\n    GridLinesStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.88]],\n    ImageSize -> 540, AspectRatio -> 0.62,\n    LabelStyle -> Directive[Black, 12],\n    Epilog -> {\n      Text[Style[eq1, 14, rule], Scaled[{0.28, 0.86}]]\n    }\n  ]\n}]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Three trials within 5%", "Section"],
Cell["The three trials kept for four filters are trials 1, 3, and 4. Their terminal speeds are 2.571391 m/s, 2.634919 m/s, and 2.535169 m/s.\n\nThe average is\n\n(2.571391 + 2.634919 + 2.535169) / 3 = 7.741479 / 3 = 2.580493 m/s.\n\nThe percent gap from that average is |Vt - 2.580493| / 2.580493 x 100%.\n\nTrial 1: |2.571391 - 2.580493| / 2.580493 x 100% = 0.35%\nTrial 3: |2.634919 - 2.580493| / 2.580493 x 100% = 2.11%\nTrial 4: |2.535169 - 2.580493| / 2.580493 x 100% = 1.76%\n\nAll three are under 5%, and the widest pair among them (trial 3 against trial 4) differs by 3.9% of the pair's mean. The four-filter speed used below is their average, 2.580 m/s.\n\nTrial 2 fitted to 2.432 m/s. That is 5.7% below this average, and it differs from trial 3 by 8.0% of the pair's mean:\n\n|2.432217 - 2.634919| / ((2.432217 + 2.634919) / 2) x 100% = 8.0%.\n\nTrial 2 was not folded into the average. Its trace is stored with the other three.", "Text"],
Cell["kept = slopes[[{1, 3, 4}]];\navg = Mean[kept];\npct = Abs[kept - avg]/avg*100;\npair23 = Abs[slopes[[2]] - slopes[[3]]]/(Mean[{slopes[[2]], slopes[[3]]}])*100;\nGrid[{\n  {\"trial\", \"Vt (m/s)\", \"% from the average of trials 1, 3, 4\", \"kept?\"},\n  {\"1\", NumberForm[slopes[[1]], {6, 4}], NumberForm[pct[[1]], {4, 2}], \"yes\"},\n  {\"2\", NumberForm[slopes[[2]], {6, 4}], NumberForm[Abs[slopes[[2]] - avg]/avg*100, {4, 2}], \"no\"},\n  {\"3\", NumberForm[slopes[[3]], {6, 4}], NumberForm[pct[[2]], {4, 2}], \"yes\"},\n  {\"4\", NumberForm[slopes[[4]], {6, 4}], NumberForm[pct[[3]], {4, 2}], \"yes\"},\n  {\"average of 1, 3, 4\", NumberForm[avg, {6, 4}], \"\", \"\"},\n  {\"trial 2 vs trial 3\", \"\", NumberForm[pair23, {4, 2}], \"pair\"}\n}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["n and b from the log-log plot", "Section"],
Cell["At terminal speed the net force is zero, so the weight and the drag are equal:\n\nM g = b Vt^n.\n\nSolving for the speed and taking log base 10 gives\n\nlog10(Vt) = (1/n) log10(M) + (1/n) log10(g/b).\n\nThe slope of log10(Vt) against log10(M) is 1/n. Call the intercept C. Then C = (1/n) log10(g/b), which rearranges to\n\nb = g / 10^(n C).\n\nThe masses were recorded in grams. Each one is divided by 1000 before the logarithm, and g is taken as 9.81 m/s^2, so b is the coefficient in F = b v^n with F in newtons and v in m/s. The four-filter mass on the sheet is 4.665 g, and its speed is the 2.580 m/s average from the three trials. The other six speeds are the reduced values already on the sheet. The open square on the plot is the four-filter point. Filled squares are the other stacks. The orange line is the fit, with its equation on the graph.", "Text"],
Cell["(* Masses in grams, as recorded. Speeds in m/s.\n   Entry 4 is the four-filter stack; its speed is the average above.\n   The other six speeds are the reduced sheet values. *)\nmassG = {1.2, 2.351, 3.5, 4.665, 2.7, 3.2, 4.3};\nvTerm = {1.25700, 2.11460, 2.43525, avg, 1.96764, 2.21563, 2.88000};\nmassKg = massG/1000;\nlogData = Transpose[{Log10[massKg], Log10[vTerm]}];\nlogFit = LinearModelFit[logData, x, x];\nslopeN = logFit[\"BestFitParameters\"][[2]];\ninterceptC = logFit[\"BestFitParameters\"][[1]];\nnExp = 1/slopeN;\nbCoeff = 9.81/10^(nExp*interceptC);\nseSlope = logFit[\"ParameterErrors\"][[2]];\nseN = seSlope/slopeN^2;\n\nlogEq = \"log10(Vt) = 0.5676 log10(M) + 1.7722\";\n\nColumn[{\n  logFit[\"ParameterTable\"],\n  Grid[{\n    {\"slope 1/n\", NumberForm[slopeN, {6, 4}]},\n    {\"intercept C\", NumberForm[interceptC, {6, 4}]},\n    {\"n = 1/slope\", NumberForm[nExp, {5, 3}]},\n    {\"uncertainty on n\", NumberForm[seN, {4, 2}]},\n    {\"b = g/10^(n C)\", ScientificForm[bCoeff, 3]},\n    {\"R^2\", NumberForm[logFit[\"RSquared\"], {6, 4}]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Show[\n    Plot[logFit[x], {x, Min[logData[[All, 1]]], Max[logData[[All, 1]]]},\n      PlotStyle -> Directive[rule, AbsoluteThickness[2.1]]\n    ],\n    ListPlot[logData,\n      PlotStyle -> RGBColor[0.16, 0.16, 0.42],\n      PlotMarkers -> {\n        Graphics[{RGBColor[0.16, 0.16, 0.42], Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}]}],\n        0.036\n      }\n    ],\n    ListPlot[{logData[[4]]},\n      PlotMarkers -> {\n        Graphics[{EdgeForm[Directive[rule, Thickness[0.12]]], FaceForm[None], Rectangle[{-1, -1}, {1, 1}]}],\n        0.058\n      }\n    ],\n    Frame -> True, Axes -> False,\n    FrameLabel -> {\"log10(M / kg)\", \"log10(Vt / (m/s))\"},\n    PlotLabel -> \"Log-log plot used for n and b\",\n    GridLines -> Automatic,\n    GridLinesStyle -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.88]],\n    ImageSize -> 540, AspectRatio -> 0.62,\n    LabelStyle -> Directive[Black, 12],\n    Epilog -> {\n      Text[Style[logEq, 12, rule], Scaled[{0.40, 0.90}]]\n    }\n  ]\n}]", "Input"],
Cell["The fit is\n\nlog10(Vt) = 0.5676 log10(M) + 1.7722,\n\nwith R^2 = 0.936.\n\nThe slope is 1/n, so\n\nn = 1 / 0.5676 = 1.762.\n\nThe standard error on the slope is 0.066. Dividing that by the slope squared puts the uncertainty on n at 0.21.\n\nThe intercept is C = 1.7722, so\n\nb = 9.81 / 10^(1.76187 x 1.77223) = 9.81 / 1325.7 = 7.40 x 10^(-3).\n\nAn exponent of 1.76 is closer to 2 than to 1, which is the direction a light, open filter should go: most of the drag is quadratic. With seven stacks the uncertainty is large enough that a pure v^2 law still sits inside the error bar. A pure linear law does not.", "Text"]
}, Open]]
},
WindowSize->{1100, 800},
WindowMargins->{{0, Automatic}, {Automatic, 0}},
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
